                             Type Conversion          
             ============================================  


coverting the the value from one datatype to another.

Their are 2 types of type Conversion
1.Implicit  - done by java conversion
2.Explicit  - done by programmer

Rules of Implicit conversion
=============================
1. value must be compatible 

ex:1
======

int n;
n='A';

sout(n)=65  As java as a numeric representation of character so 'A' will be converted in to 65 

ex:2
======

int n;
n=true; Error  java does not have any numeric representation of boolean value


2. RHS must be smaller than LHS

ex:1
====

int a;
a='Z';

ex:2
====

int s=2.3; Error

message
=======
possible lossy conversion from double to int


Solution
==========

Explicit Conversion

int s=(int)2.7

sout(s)=2


